  "Question": "When finding the sum\n\n\\[\\dfrac12 + \\dfrac13 + \\dfrac14 + \\dfrac15 + \\dfrac16 + \\dfrac17,\\]\n\nwhat is the least common denominator used?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(120\\)",
    "B": "\\(210\\)",
    "C": "\\(420\\)",
    "D": "\\(840\\)",
    "E": "\\(5040\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The least common denominator is the smallest positive whole number divisible by every denominator: \\(2,3,4,5,6,7\\).\n\nDivisibility by \\(4=2\\cdot2\\) requires two factors of \\(2\\). We also need factors of \\(3\\), \\(5\\), and \\(7\\). Thus every common denominator must be a multiple of\n\\[2\\cdot2\\cdot3\\cdot5\\cdot7=420.\\]\nThis product is divisible by \\(2\\) and by \\(6=2\\cdot3\\) as well, so it satisfies every requirement. The least common denominator is \\(420\\), choice C.",
